          "text": "Postnatal timing and infant feeding"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Three months postnatal; first baby, delivered by NSVD; breastfeeding and using formula."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-2",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Low mood and depressive symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "For 6–8 weeks: increased low mood, anhedonia, fatigue, poor concentration, and crying most days."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-3",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-3",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Intrusive thoughts and images of harming the baby"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Intrusive, ego-dystonic images of harming the baby, including on stairs and by smothering. Patient is very distressed, says she would never do it, has no plan or intent, is scared of the thoughts rather than the baby, and avoids being alone with the baby."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-4",
